  "result": "I added a hook that runs Prettier whenever I edit or write a TypeScript file. I haven't tested it, and it won't format anything until Prettier is installed in the project.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **`.claude/settings.json`**: added a hook that runs after every Edit or Write, next to your existing `block-rm` hook.\n- **`.claude/hooks/format-ts.mjs`**: the new script. It only acts on `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.mts` and `.cts` files and runs `npx --no-install prettier --write <file>` on them. If Prettier fails, the error is shown but the edit still goes through.\n\n**To make it work:** Prettier isn't in `package.json`. I set it up so it never downloads Prettier by itself, which would be slow on every edit. Until you install it, every TypeScript edit will show a \"Prettier failed\" message. To install it:\n\n```sh\nnpm install --save-dev prettier\n```\n\nYou may also want a `.prettierrc`; without one, Prettier uses its default style.\n\nI didn't run `npm run lint` or `npm run build`, since this change doesn't touch any app code.",
